1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,425
Numbers racing down the screen. Price, size, price, size.

2
00:00:11,876 --> 00:00:17,988
Two lots, one lot, three lots. And suddenly, one hundred fifty lots.

3
00:00:18,439 --> 00:00:22,305
What is this crowd saying? Today we learn to read it.

4
00:00:23,305 --> 00:00:28,216
Hello, this is episode eleven of the SPIDER Order Flow series.

5
00:00:28,665 --> 00:00:32,793
Last time: Market Profile and the types of days.

6
00:00:33,243 --> 00:00:39,513
Today real order flow begins. Step one: Time and Sales, the tape.

7
00:00:40,513 --> 00:00:43,099
The tape is one line for every trade that happens.

8
00:00:43,549 --> 00:00:49,191
Each line has four things: time, price, size and side.

9
00:00:49,641 --> 00:00:55,597
The order book shows who is waiting. The tape shows what actually traded.

10
00:00:56,597 --> 00:00:59,183
Side means: who was in a hurry?

11
00:00:59,633 --> 00:01:04,700
If it traded at the ask, a buyer used a market order. That is green.

12
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:09,984
If it traded at the bid, a seller used a market order. That is red.

13
00:01:10,434 --> 00:01:16,860
Remember episode three: the market order is in a hurry, the limit order is waiting.

14
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:22,771
Most lines are small: one, two, five lots.

15
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:28,785
When one line is suddenly fifty times the usual size, that is a big print.

16
00:01:29,235 --> 00:01:34,303
But remember: big players often split their order into small pieces.

17
00:01:34,753 --> 00:01:41,100
So more important than one big line is many lines hitting the same price again and again.

18
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,294
The speed of the tape also says something.

19
00:01:44,744 --> 00:01:51,092
A slow tape, one line every few seconds: interest is low right now.

20
00:01:51,541 --> 00:01:57,262
A fast tape, dozens of lines a second: something big is happening.

21
00:01:58,262 --> 00:02:04,140
A fast tape comes in two forms. First: the tape is fast, but price is not moving.

22
00:02:04,591 --> 00:02:11,357
Green lines are pouring in, buyers keep buying, yet price is stuck at the same level.

23
00:02:11,807 --> 00:02:17,370
It means a big limit seller above is soaking it all up. This is absorption.

24
00:02:18,370 --> 00:02:23,438
Second form: the tape is fast and price moves fast in one direction.

25
00:02:23,888 --> 00:02:29,374
Each new line prints beyond the last price. The resting limit orders keep getting used up.

26
00:02:29,823 --> 00:02:35,310
Here the aggressive players are winning. Moves like this often carry for a while.

27
00:02:36,310 --> 00:02:40,829
An important truth: spot forex has no real tape.

28
00:02:41,279 --> 00:02:47,156
Forex does not trade on one exchange. Your broker only shows its own slice.

29
00:02:47,607 --> 00:02:54,033
For a real tape, look at futures such as gold or index futures, or a crypto exchange.

30
00:02:55,033 --> 00:03:00,283
Now the problem: in a fast market, thousands of lines a minute.

31
00:03:00,733 --> 00:03:04,599
Your eyes get tired, and the full picture never forms.

32
00:03:05,049 --> 00:03:12,285
The fix: the same data, added up at each price inside one candle. That is a footprint.

33
00:03:13,285 --> 00:03:17,256
An example. Price is near resistance at 100.

34
00:03:17,706 --> 00:03:23,739
The tape is fast. Green lines keep printing at 100, but 100 does not break.

35
00:03:24,190 --> 00:03:28,631
Then suddenly red lines start, and price slips lower.

36
00:03:29,081 --> 00:03:35,768
Buyers pushed, but the seller above won. This is a scenario, not a guarantee.

37
00:03:36,768 --> 00:03:38,257
So, today's summary.

38
00:03:38,707 --> 00:03:46,988
The tape is a line per trade: time, price, size, side. At the ask is green, at the bid is red.

39
00:03:47,438 --> 00:03:53,316
Watch big prints and repeated lines at one price. Read the tape speed too.

40
00:03:53,766 --> 00:04:00,609
Fast tape with stuck price means absorption. Spot forex has no real tape.

41
00:04:01,609 --> 00:04:05,241
Next episode: how to read a footprint chart.

42
